{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.089,
            0.74,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "Now we divide this $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ into 2 equal parts. What do we get? What fraction of the whole is shaded?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.147,
            0.325,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.12,
                0.28,
                0.331,
                0.306
              ],
              "content": "$\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ divided into 2 equal parts"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.375,
            0.152,
            0.848,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": "Since the whole is divided into 8 equal parts and one of the parts is shaded, we can say that $\\frac { 1 } { 8 }$ of the whole is shaded. So, the distance covered by the tortoise in half an hour is $\\frac { 1 } { 8 }$ km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.4,
            0.27,
            0.661,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": "This tells us that ${ \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } = { \\frac { 1 } { 8 } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.312,
            0.848,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "? If the tortoise walks faster and it can cover $\\frac{2}{5}$ km in 1 hour, how far will it walk in $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ of an hour?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.388,
            0.4,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered $= { \\frac { 3 } { 4 } } \\times { \\frac { 2 } { 5 } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.436,
            0.373,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": "**Finding the product:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.471,
            0.667,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "(i) First find the distance covered in $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ of an hour."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.506,
            0.847,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Multiply the result by 3, to get the distance covered in $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ of an hour."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.567,
            0.602,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "(i) Distance in km covered in $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ of an hour = The quantity we get by dividing $\\frac{2}{5}$ into 4 equal parts."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.652,
            0.604,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "Taking the unit square as the whole, the shaded part (in Fig. 8.1) is a region we get when we divide $\\frac{2}{5}$ into 4 equal parts."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.644,
            0.589,
            0.851,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.739,
            0.481,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": "How much of the whole is it? The whole is divided into 5 rows and 4 columns, creating $5 \\times 4 = 2 0$ equal parts."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.695,
            0.757,
            0.756,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 8.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.823,
            0.515,
            0.843
          ],
          "content": "Number of these parts shaded = 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.845,
            0.624,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": "So, the distance covered in $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ of an hour $c = { \\frac { 2 } { 2 0 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.938,
            0.192,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": "178"
        },
        {
